WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.567
Here's one,

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:10.033
a picture puzzle!

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.467
Which shape completes the pattern?

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:12.967
A.

00:00:12.967 --> 00:00:14.433
A filled circle,

00:00:14.433 --> 00:00:14.933
B.

00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:16.400
A filled square,

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:16.867
C.

00:00:16.867 --> 00:00:18.333
An empty square,

00:00:18.333 --> 00:00:19.333
or D.

00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:20.800
A filled triangle?

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.767
Five seconds!

00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:28.733
TIME'S UP!

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:30.567
The answer is...

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:30.933
B,

00:00:30.933 --> 00:00:32.100
a filled square!

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.400
The rule is the shape gets

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.733
filled in but stays the same

00:00:36.733 --> 00:00:37.100
shape,

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.433
so the empty square becomes a

00:00:39.433 --> 00:00:40.200
filled square.

00:00:41.367 --> 00:00:41.967
Alright,

00:00:41.967 --> 00:00:43.767
a word analogy!

00:00:43.767 --> 00:00:46.133
Pen is to write,

00:00:46.133 --> 00:00:48.533
as scissors is to...

00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:49.133
what?

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:49.733
A.

00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:50.333
Paper,

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:50.900
B.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:51.500
Cut,

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.100
C.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:52.700
Sharp,

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.900
or D.

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:54.500
Glue?

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.700
Five seconds!

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:02.667
TIME'S UP!

00:01:03.333 --> 00:01:03.733
It's...

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:04.133
B,

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:04.533
cut!

00:01:04.533 --> 00:01:06.933
A pen is used to write,

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:09.333
so scissors are used to cut.

00:01:09.333 --> 00:01:12.133
It is the job each tool does.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:13.833
Okay,

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:15.400
a number series!

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:15.933
Two,

00:01:15.933 --> 00:01:16.467
six,

00:01:16.467 --> 00:01:16.967
eighteen,

00:01:16.967 --> 00:01:17.500
fifty-four,

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.567
and then...

00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.133
what comes next?

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:20.667
A.

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.233
One hundred eight,

00:01:22.233 --> 00:01:22.767
B.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.333
One hundred sixty-two,

00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:24.867
C.

00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:26.433
One hundred fifty,

00:01:26.433 --> 00:01:27.467
or D.

00:01:27.467 --> 00:01:29.067
Two hundred sixteen?

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.100
Five seconds!

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.100
TIME'S UP!

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:39.400
The answer is...

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:39.933
B,

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:41.567
one hundred sixty-two!

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:44.800
Each number is multiplied by three:

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.333
two,

00:01:45.333 --> 00:01:45.867
six,

00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:46.433
eighteen,

00:01:46.433 --> 00:01:46.967
fifty-four,

00:01:46.967 --> 00:01:50.200
so fifty-four times three is one

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.300
hundred sixty-two.

00:01:52.433 --> 00:01:52.967
Okay,

00:01:52.967 --> 00:01:54.600
a picture puzzle!

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.833
Where does the dot move next?

00:01:57.833 --> 00:01:58.400
A.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:01:58.933
Top-left,

00:01:58.933 --> 00:01:59.467
B.

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:00.000
Bottom-right,

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.533
C.

00:02:00.533 --> 00:02:01.100
Center,

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.167
or D.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:02.700
Top-right?

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:03.800
Five seconds!

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.767
TIME'S UP!

00:02:11.433 --> 00:02:13.100
The answer is...

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:13.667
B,

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:14.233
bottom-right!

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.467
The dot steps counter-clockwise

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:18.167
corner to corner:

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:18.700
top-right,

00:02:18.700 --> 00:02:19.267
top-left,

00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:19.833
bottom-left,

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:23.200
so the next corner is bottom-right.

00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:24.967
Alright!

00:02:24.967 --> 00:02:28.200
Which one does NOT belong?

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:28.833
A.

00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:29.500
Copper,

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:30.133
B.

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:30.767
Gold,

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:31.433
C.

00:02:31.433 --> 00:02:32.067
Wood,

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.367
or D.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:34.000
Silver?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.300
Five seconds!

00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:42.267
TIME'S UP!

00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:43.400
It's...

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:43.900
C,

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:44.367
wood!

00:02:44.367 --> 00:02:44.867
Copper,

00:02:44.867 --> 00:02:45.333
gold,

00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:47.733
and silver are all metals.

00:02:47.733 --> 00:02:49.667
Wood comes from trees,

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.067
so it does not belong.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.500
Here's one,

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:56.467
a number series!

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:57.100
Three,

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:57.767
five,

00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:58.433
nine,

00:02:58.433 --> 00:02:59.067
fifteen,

00:02:59.067 --> 00:02:59.733
twenty-three,

00:02:59.733 --> 00:03:01.033
and then...

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.000
what comes next?

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:03.633
A.

00:03:03.633 --> 00:03:04.300
Thirty-one,

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:04.933
B.

00:03:04.933 --> 00:03:05.600
Thirty-two,

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:06.233
C.

00:03:06.233 --> 00:03:06.900
Thirty-five,

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.200
or D.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:08.867
Thirty-three?

00:03:08.867 --> 00:03:10.167
Five seconds!

00:03:15.933 --> 00:03:17.133
TIME'S UP!

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:19.467
The answer is...

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:20.000
D,

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:20.567
thirty-three!

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:23.333
The gaps grow by two:

00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:24.433
plus two,

00:03:24.433 --> 00:03:25.000
four,

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:25.533
six,

00:03:25.533 --> 00:03:26.100
eight,

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.767
then plus ten.

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:31.067
So twenty-three plus ten is thirty-three.

00:03:32.233 --> 00:03:33.233
Here's one,

00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:34.767
a shape puzzle!

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.767
Which shape comes next?

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:37.267
A.

00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.267
A pentagon,

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:38.767
B.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:39.800
A circle,

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:40.300
C.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.300
A hexagon,

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.300
or D.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.300
A square?

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:44.300
Five seconds!

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.300
TIME'S UP!

00:03:51.967 --> 00:03:53.400
The answer is...

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:53.900
A,

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:54.867
a pentagon!

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.767
The sides count down by one:

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:58.733
octagon eight,

00:03:58.733 --> 00:03:59.700
heptagon seven,

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:00.667
hexagon six,

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.567
so next is the pentagon with

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:04.533
five sides.

00:04:05.667 --> 00:04:06.367
Alright,

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:08.400
a number analogy!

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.467
Two makes eight,

00:04:10.467 --> 00:04:12.533
three makes twelve,

00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:14.567
four makes sixteen,

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.633
so five makes...

00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:17.333
what?

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:18.000
A.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:18.700
Twenty,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:19.367
B.

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:20.067
Eighteen,

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:20.767
C.

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:21.433
Twenty-four,

00:04:21.433 --> 00:04:22.800
or D.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:23.500
Fifteen?

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:24.867
Five seconds!

00:04:30.667 --> 00:04:31.867
TIME'S UP!

00:04:32.533 --> 00:04:33.100
It's...

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:33.700
A,

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:34.267
twenty!

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:37.733
Each number is multiplied by four:

00:04:37.733 --> 00:04:40.600
five times four is twenty.

00:04:41.767 --> 00:04:43.100
Check this out,

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.900
fill in the blank!

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.600
The museum guide gave such a

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.267
blank talk that nobody in the

00:04:50.267 --> 00:04:52.533
group wanted it to end.

00:04:52.533 --> 00:04:52.967
A.

00:04:52.967 --> 00:04:53.400
Boring,

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:53.867
B.

00:04:53.867 --> 00:04:54.300
Quiet,

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:54.767
C.

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:55.200
Short,

00:04:55.200 --> 00:04:56.100
or D.

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:56.567
Fascinating?

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:57.433
Five seconds!

00:05:03.233 --> 00:05:04.433
TIME'S UP!

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:05.600
It's...

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.067
D,

00:05:06.067 --> 00:05:06.567
fascinating!

00:05:06.567 --> 00:05:09.533
If nobody wanted the talk to

00:05:09.533 --> 00:05:10.000
end,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.967
it was very interesting.

00:05:11.967 --> 00:05:13.933
Fascinating means so interesting

00:05:13.933 --> 00:05:15.900
you cannot look away.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.100
Here's one,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.667
a number puzzle,

00:05:19.667 --> 00:05:21.267
and it's sneaky!

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:24.400
If one plus two makes nine,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:27.000
two plus three makes fifteen,

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.633
four plus one makes fifteen,

00:05:29.633 --> 00:05:32.233
then three plus three makes...

00:05:32.233 --> 00:05:32.767
what?

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:33.267
A.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:33.800
Nine,

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.333
B.

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:34.833
Twelve,

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:35.367
C.

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:35.900
Eighteen,

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:36.933
or D.

00:05:36.933 --> 00:05:37.467
Six?

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:38.500
Five seconds!

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.500
TIME'S UP!

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.567
The answer is...

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:48.033
C,

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:48.500
eighteen!

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:50.367
Add the two numbers,

00:05:50.367 --> 00:05:52.233
then multiply by three:

00:05:52.233 --> 00:05:54.567
three plus three is six,

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:57.367
and six times three is eighteen.

00:05:58.533 --> 00:05:58.933
So,

00:05:58.933 --> 00:06:00.967
are you smart or fart?

00:06:00.967 --> 00:06:03.400
Count up your correct answers to

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.600
find your rank!

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:06.133
So,

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:07.567
how did you do?

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:09.033
Comment your score below,

00:06:09.033 --> 00:06:10.500
and subscribe for more!
